<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43626" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐδιά-θετος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>well-arranged.</i>
			Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τως</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>BJ</u>
				3.5.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>easily affected</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ τῶν ἔξωθεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.D.
					<u>Synt.</u>
					291.15
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>well-disposed</i>, of persons. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τως</span>, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐγνωμόνως</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>easy to dispose of</i> (in marriage), Id.
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ εὐ</span>
			.; also of arguments or objections, <i><span class="en">
				Them.
				<u>in APo.</u>
				62.33
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>